  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV prevention in Indigenous community</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main focus of the project will be on reducing sexual violence and improving HIV-related healthcare (including prevention of sexually transmitted diseases) in indigenous communities in the northern Cauca, Colombia. 

La Asociaci&#xF3;n de Cabildos Ind&#xED;genas del Norte del Cauca &#x2013;ACIN is the coordinating body for the Cabildos or authorities of 18 indigenous reserves/resguardos, and runs a wide range of education, health, gender and sustainable development programmes. Its health programme, seeks to promote health and prevent infections in a manner that is culturally sensitive and respectful of the traditional approaches of the indigenous people it serves. 

The HIV and AIDS project which CAFOD supports is able to coordinate with the other programmes to provide a more holistic approach. There are currently very few projects in Colombia that are addressing HIV and AIDS within indigenous communities. The work that CAFOD has funded with ACIN adopted an innovative approach looking at root causes of the spread of HIV and sexually transmitted infections, such as domestic violence and the sexual abuse of women. The project has been successful in working in a respectful but challenging way to raise issues that until recently, were rarely acknowledged within the Nasa indigenous community.</narrative>
  </description>
